// arXiv source page 2
#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(294.65pt, 790.176pt, "2 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 14.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 83.88pt, "Abstract ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.824pt, 114.26pt, "Magnetic skyrmions, renowned for their fascinating electromagnetic properties, hold potential ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 141.86pt, "for next-generation topological spintronic devices. Recent advancements have unveiled a rich ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 169.46pt, "tapestry of 3D topological magnetism. Nevertheless, the practical application of 3D ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 197.06pt, "topological magnetism in the development of topological spintronic devices remains a ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 224.66pt, "challenge. Here, we showcase the experimental utilization of 3D topological magnetism ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 252.26pt, "through the exploitation of skyrmion-edge attractive interactions in 90-nm-wide confined ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 279.89pt, "chiral FeGe and CoZnMn magnetic nanostructures. These attractive interactions result in two ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 307.49pt, "degenerate equilibrium positions, which can be naturally interpreted as binary bits for a ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 335.09pt, "skyrmion sliding switch. Our theory and simulation reveal current-driven spiral motions of ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 362.69pt, "skyrmions, governed by the anisotropic gradient of the potential landscape. Our experiments ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 390.29pt, "validate the theory that predicts a tunable threshold current density via magnetic field and ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 417.89pt, "temperature modulation of the energy barrier. Our results offer an approach for implementing ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 445.37pt, "universal on-off switch functions in 3D topological spintronic devices. ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 500.59pt, "Keywords: magnetic skyrmions; chiral magnetic nanostructures; current-controlled sliding ")
  #line-at(70.824pt, 528.19pt, "switch; 3D magnetism ")
]

