  #line-at(70.104pt, 247.58pt, "has profoundly enriched the functionality of topological spintronics.  ")
  #line-at(94.104pt, 275.18pt, "The intricate 3D spin twists observed in conical magnetizations of chiral magnets lead to ")
  #line-at(70.104pt, 302.81pt, "distinctive attractive interactions between topological solitons and boundary geometries.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(517.18pt, 298.25pt, "26")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(70.104pt, 330.41pt, "These interactions offer promising avenues for the development of innovative nanoelectronic ")
  #line-at(70.104pt, 358.01pt, "devices. For instance, theoretical simulations indicate that magnetic attractive interactions in ")
  #line-at(70.104pt, 385.61pt, "3D confined chiral magnet geometries can naturally induce the formation of binary channels ")
  #line-at(70.104pt, 413.21pt, "near edges.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(125.18pt, 408.65pt, "27")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(133.34pt, 413.21pt, " The binary channels can serve as natural patterning in multi-channel racetrack ")
  #line-at(70.104pt, 440.81pt, "memories or provide an alternative skyrmion switch. The on/off switching functionality of ")
  #line-at(70.104pt, 468.43pt, "topological spintronic devices is typically achieved through topological transformations ")
  #line-at(70.104pt, 496.03pt, "between skyrmions and saturated states with uniformed magnetizations.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(421.75pt, 491.47pt, "28-32")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(440.5pt, 496.03pt, " However, due to ")
  #line-at(70.104pt, 523.63pt, "the distinctly different configurations between skyrmions and saturated states, there are ")
  #line-at(70.104pt, 551.23pt, "significant energy differences,")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(219.77pt, 546.67pt, "30, 31")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(241.73pt, 551.23pt, " necessitating asymmetrical physical conditions, such as ")
  #line-at(70.104pt, 578.83pt, "tailored magnetic fields")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(197.45pt, 574.27pt, "28-31")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(216.17pt, 578.83pt, " and current profiles")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(334.15pt, 574.27pt, "32")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(342.31pt, 578.83pt, ", for current-controlled skyrmion-")
  #line-at(70.104pt, 606.43pt, "ferromagnet transformations. The binary channels facilitate the realization of an alternative ")
  #line-at(70.104pt, 634.03pt, "on/off switch, i.e. skyrmion sliding on/off switch, relying on current-induced motions of the ")
  #line-at(70.104pt, 661.66pt, "skyrmion between predefined equilibrium positions. While experimental studies have ")
  #line-at(70.104pt, 689.26pt, "predominantly focused on the current-driven dynamic motion of skyrmions in open ")
  #line-at(70.104pt, 716.86pt, "geometries,")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
