#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-04.png", width: 455pt), 70pt, 71pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(294.65pt, 790.176pt, "4 ")
  #line-at(94.104pt, 81.96pt, "Here, we delve into the stabilization and current-induced dynamics of a single skyrmion ")
  #line-at(70.104pt, 109.58pt, "confined within geometrically constrained stripes of chiral magnets. Leveraging 3D ")
  #line-at(70.104pt, 137.18pt, "topological magnetism, we experimentally discern two degenerate equilibrium positions for ")
  #line-at(70.104pt, 164.78pt, "skyrmions confined within a nanostructure, stemming from the attractions between the ")
  #line-at(70.104pt, 192.38pt, "skyrmion and the edges. Furthermore, we achieve the controlled motions of a single skyrmion ")
  #line-at(70.104pt, 219.98pt, "between these two equilibrium positions utilizing ultrafast single-pulse currents. Our ")
  #line-at(70.104pt, 247.58pt, "approach, which realizes the on/off switch function through the utilization of 3D topological ")
  #line-at(70.104pt, 275.18pt, "magnetism, as opposed to the traditional creation/erasion of skyrmions, could inspire ")
  #line-at(70.104pt, 302.81pt, "advanced designs for topological spintronic devices. ")
  #line-at(94.104pt, 330.41pt, "Figure 1a illustrates the schematic design of the skyrmion sliding switch. With a width of ")
  #line-at(70.104pt, 358.01pt, "100 nm, it enables the confinement of a single row of skyrmions within the nanostructured ")
  #line-at(70.104pt, 385.61pt, "FeGe stripe.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(128.66pt, 381.05pt, "39")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(136.82pt, 385.61pt, " Due to attractions between the skyrmion and the edge in the conical background ")
